00:02:21.841 --> 00:02:23.009
HARD WORK ON THIS BILL. AS THE

00:02:23.076 --> 00:02:24.811
NUMBER OF CALIFORNIA IS

00:02:24.878 --> 00:02:25.812
PRESENTING IN PSYCHIATRIC IN A

00:02:25.879 --> 00:02:28.414
PSYCHIATRIC CRISIS CONTINUES TO

00:02:28.481 --> 00:02:29.349
INCREASE, HOSPITAL EMERGENCY

00:02:29.415 --> 00:02:30.250
DEPARTMENTS HAVE BECOME A

00:02:30.316 --> 00:02:32.952
CRITICAL PART OF THE SAFETY NET

00:02:33.019 --> 00:02:34.087
FOR INDIVIDUALS WHO DESPERATELY

00:02:34.153 --> 00:02:35.922
NEED PSYCHIATRIC TREATMENT. IN

00:02:35.989 --> 00:02:39.659
RECENT YEARS, THOUGH, COUNTIES

00:02:39.726 --> 00:02:40.660
HAVE INSTRUCTED HOSPITALS TO

00:02:40.727 --> 00:02:42.128
HOLD A PATIENT IN THE EMERGENCY

00:02:42.195 --> 00:02:43.196
DEPARTMENT IF THE PATIENT IS ON

00:02:43.263 --> 00:02:45.164
AN INVOLUNTARY PSYCHIATRIC HOLD,

00:02:45.231 --> 00:02:48.701
OR IF THE PATIENT HAS MEDI-CAL,

00:02:48.768 --> 00:02:49.235
LEADING TO UNNECESSARILY,

00:02:49.302 --> 00:02:54.240
PROLONGED STAYS IN THE EMERGENCY

00:02:54.307 --> 00:02:55.241
DEPARTMENT. IN FACT, DATA

00:02:55.308 --> 00:02:58.144
SUGGESTS THAT ABOUT 25% OF

00:02:58.211 --> 00:02:59.646
INDIVIDUALS BROUGHT TO THE

00:02:59.712 --> 00:03:00.146
EMERGENCY DEPARTMENT IN

00:03:00.213 --> 00:03:01.948
PSYCHIATRIC CRISIS REMAIN THERE

00:03:02.015 --> 00:03:03.216
FOR THREE OR MORE DAYS. THIS HAS

00:03:03.283 --> 00:03:05.385
LED TO VALUABLE EMERGENCY

00:03:05.451 --> 00:03:07.020
DEPARTMENT SPACE BEING TAKEN UP

00:03:07.086 --> 00:03:08.588
IN HOSPITALS ACROSS THE STATE.

00:03:08.655 --> 00:03:11.424
AB 1316 WOULD ADDRESS THIS

00:03:11.491 --> 00:03:12.425
ISSUE, CLARIFYING THAT HOSPITALS

00:03:12.492 --> 00:03:14.127
MAY ARRANGE A TIMELY AND

00:03:14.193 --> 00:03:15.128
APPROPRIATE TRANSFER FOR

00:03:15.194 --> 00:03:17.931
PATIENTS REQUIRING INPATIENT

00:03:17.997 --> 00:03:19.032
PSYCHIATRIC CARE TO THE FIRST

00:03:19.098 --> 00:03:21.334
AVAILABLE BED IN AN INPATIENT

00:03:21.401 --> 00:03:22.335
FACILITY, REGARDLESS OF PAYER

00:03:22.402 --> 00:03:24.504
PREFERENCE. THIS BILL ALSO

00:03:24.571 --> 00:03:25.538
CLARIFIES THAT MEDI-CAL MANAGED

00:03:25.605 --> 00:03:27.907
CARE PLANS MUST PAY EMERGENCY

00:03:27.974 --> 00:03:28.908
DEPARTMENTS FOR THE CARE THEY

00:03:28.975 --> 00:03:31.544
PROVIDE TO MEDI-CAL

00:03:31.611 --> 00:03:32.345
BENEFICIARIES EXPERIENCING A

00:03:32.412 --> 00:03:35.281
MENTAL HEALTH CRISIS. THIS WOULD

00:03:35.348 --> 00:03:38.451
CODIFY AN EXISTING DCS POLICY

00:03:38.518 --> 00:03:39.619
THAT SOUGHT TO ENSURE HOSPITALS

00:03:39.686 --> 00:03:42.055
ARE PAID FOR THE MENTAL HEALTH

00:03:42.121 --> 00:03:43.756
CARE SERVICES THEY PROVIDE. I

00:03:43.823 --> 00:03:45.224
WOULD LIKE TO NOTE THAT MY

00:03:45.291 --> 00:03:46.426
OFFICE AND THE BILL'S SPONSOR

00:03:46.492 --> 00:03:49.162
HAVE HAD POSITIVE CONVERSATIONS

00:03:49.228 --> 00:03:50.029
WITH THE OPPOSITION'S ABOUT

00:03:50.096 --> 00:03:51.097
THEIR CONCERNS WITH THE BILL,

00:03:51.164 --> 00:03:52.799
AND I LOOK FORWARD TO CONTINUING

00:03:52.865 --> 00:03:53.800
THESE CONVERSATIONS WITH THE

00:03:53.866 --> 00:03:55.568
HOPES OF RESOLVING THESE

00:03:55.635 --> 00:03:58.471
CONCERNS WITH ME TO TESTIFY IN

00:03:58.538 --> 00:03:59.572
SUPPORT OF THE BILL. AS

00:03:59.639 --> 00:04:00.640
CHRISTINE BARLOW, ON BEHALF OF

00:04:00.707 --> 00:04:01.908
THE CALIFORNIA HOSPITAL

00:04:01.975 --> 00:04:05.278
ASSOCIATION, AND RANDALL HAGER,

00:04:05.345 --> 00:04:06.446
ON BEHALF OF THE PSYCHIATRIC

00:04:06.512 --> 00:04:08.648
PHYSICIANS ALLIANCE OF

00:04:08.715 --> 00:04:09.716
CALIFORNIA. THANK YOU. PLEASE

00:04:09.782 --> 00:04:12.719
PROCEED WHEN READY. GOOD

00:04:12.785 --> 00:04:13.753
AFTERNOON, KIRSTEN BARLOW WITH

00:04:13.820 --> 00:04:15.888
THE CALIFORNIA HOSPITAL

00:04:15.955 --> 00:04:16.823
ASSOCIATION, A SPONSOR OF THE

00:04:16.889 --> 00:04:19.926
BILL, THANK YOU FOR YOUR TIME

00:04:19.993 --> 00:04:21.094
THIS AFTERNOON. AND AS MENTIONED

00:04:21.160 --> 00:04:23.262
BY OUR AUTHOR, AS MANY AS 1 IN 5

00:04:23.329 --> 00:04:25.765
PEOPLE WHO COME TO AN EMERGENCY

00:04:25.832 --> 00:04:27.033
ROOM ON ANY GIVEN DAY, ARE THERE

00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:28.801
ACTUALLY SEEKING MENTAL HEALTH

00:04:28.868 --> 00:04:29.869
CRISIS ASSISTANCE. AND WHILE THE

00:04:29.936 --> 00:04:33.539
NATIONAL STANDARD OF WHAT ANY OF

00:04:33.606 --> 00:04:34.707
US SHOULD EXPECT WHEN WE GO TO

00:04:34.774 --> 00:04:36.042
AN EMERGENCY ROOM MIGHT BE THAT

00:04:36.109 --> 00:04:37.777
YOU'RE IN, YOU'RE ABLE TO GET

00:04:37.844 --> 00:04:39.345
TRIAGED AND TREATED WITHIN ABOUT

00:04:39.412 --> 00:04:40.580
FOUR HOURS. AS WAS MENTIONED

00:04:40.647 --> 00:04:43.149
BEFORE, IT'S NOT UNCOMMON,

00:04:43.216 --> 00:04:44.217
UNFORTUNATELY, FOR FOLKS TO WIND

00:04:44.283 --> 00:04:45.752
UP STAYING FOR, MANY HOURS, IF

00:04:45.818 --> 00:04:49.255
NOT EVEN DAYS OR WEEKS, WHILE

00:04:49.322 --> 00:04:50.223
TREATMENT IS SOUGHT AND A

00:04:50.289 --> 00:04:52.191
PLACEMENT AVAILABLE FOR SOMEONE

00:04:52.258 --> 00:04:53.459
IN A CRISIS, I THINK WE WANTED

00:04:53.526 --> 00:04:57.196
TO REALLY TRY TO ENSURE THAT WE

00:04:57.263 --> 00:04:58.398
HAVE A STATEWIDE APPROACH TO HOW

00:04:58.464 --> 00:04:59.866
FOLKS ARE BEING HANDLED WHEN

00:04:59.932 --> 00:05:01.034
THEY ARE IN AN INPATIENT

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:02.235
EMERGENCY OR IN A PSYCHIATRIC

00:05:02.301 --> 00:05:05.638
EMERGENCY, AND TO ENSURE THAT

00:05:05.705 --> 00:05:06.139
WE'RE TREATING EMERGENCY

00:05:06.205 --> 00:05:06.973
PSYCHIATRIC CONDITIONS THE SAME

00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:10.176
WAY ANY ONE OF US WOULD

00:05:10.243 --> 00:05:11.177
EXPERIENCE AN EMERGENCY ROOM

00:05:11.244 --> 00:05:12.412
VISIT FOR A MEDICAL CONDITION,

00:05:12.478 --> 00:05:14.447
WHICH IS THAT YOU WOULD BE

00:05:14.514 --> 00:05:17.316
IMMEDIATELY SEEN. AND IF YOU

00:05:17.383 --> 00:05:19.052
CAN'T BE STABILIZED OR TREATED

00:05:19.118 --> 00:05:20.119
THERE AT THAT HOSPITAL, YOU

00:05:20.186 --> 00:05:21.154
WOULD IMMEDIATELY, YOU KNOW,

00:05:21.220 --> 00:05:22.255
EFFORTS WOULD BE UNDERTAKEN

00:05:22.321 --> 00:05:23.623
IMMEDIATELY TO GET YOU

00:05:23.690 --> 00:05:24.657
TRANSFERRED, UNDER FEDERAL LAW,

00:05:24.724 --> 00:05:26.426
REALLY, HOSPITALS ARE SUPPOSED

00:05:26.492 --> 00:05:28.194
TO BE DOING THIS WITH ANY

00:05:28.261 --> 00:05:29.328
PATIENT WHO PRESENTS TO THE

00:05:29.395 --> 00:05:30.496
EMERGENCY ROOM AND HEALTH PLANS

00:05:30.563 --> 00:05:32.765
OR PAYERS ARE PROHIBITED FROM

00:05:32.832 --> 00:05:37.403
REQUIRING THAT PRE-AUTHORIZATION

00:05:37.470 --> 00:05:38.604
TO HAPPEN FOR THAT TREATMENT,

00:05:38.671 --> 00:05:40.239
INCLUDING FOR ANYONE TO BE

00:05:40.306 --> 00:05:41.340
GETTING EMERGENCY PSYCHIATRIC

00:05:41.407 --> 00:05:43.443
CARE. SO AB 1316 WOULD ENSURE

00:05:43.509 --> 00:05:46.946
PATIENTS AND HOSPITAL ERS ARE NO

00:05:47.013 --> 00:05:47.980
LONGER TREATED DIFFERENTLY THAN

00:05:48.047 --> 00:05:49.048
ANY OTHER TYPE OF MEDICAL

00:05:49.115 --> 00:05:51.050
EMERGENCY THAT PRESENTS IN THE

00:05:51.117 --> 00:05:52.218
ER. AND THEN SECONDLY, IT CLEARS

00:05:52.285 --> 00:05:54.253
UP A LONG STANDING, SET OF,

00:05:54.320 --> 00:05:57.156
UNCLEAR GUIDANCE ABOUT MEDI-CAL

00:05:57.223 --> 00:05:58.024
BENEFICIARIES THAT WHEN THEY

00:05:58.091 --> 00:06:00.226
COME TO THE EMERGENCY ROOM

00:06:00.293 --> 00:06:01.294
SEEKING MENTAL HEALTH CARE, WHO

00:06:01.360 --> 00:06:03.529
WHICH SYSTEM ARE WE SUPPOSED TO

00:06:03.596 --> 00:06:05.331
HAVE PAY FOR THAT SERVICE? AND

00:06:05.398 --> 00:06:07.133
SO IT'S THE INTENT OF OUR BILL

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:10.236
TO CODIFY INTO STATE LAW, A

00:06:10.303 --> 00:06:11.471
POLICY OF THE STATE DEPARTMENT

00:06:11.537 --> 00:06:13.506
OF HEALTH CARE SERVICES THAT OUR

00:06:13.573 --> 00:06:14.674
MEDI-CAL MANAGED CARE PLANS, NOT

00:06:14.741 --> 00:06:17.944
THE COUNTY MENTAL HEALTH SYSTEM,

00:06:18.010 --> 00:06:18.911
BE RESPONSIBLE FOR THOSE

00:06:18.978 --> 00:06:20.379
EMERGENCY ROOM SERVICES. SO

00:06:20.446 --> 00:06:21.447
THANK YOU SO MUCH FOR

00:06:21.514 --> 00:06:23.783
CONSIDERING TODAY. AND AS WAS

00:06:23.850 --> 00:06:24.884
MENTIONED, WE ARE TALKING WITH

00:06:24.951 --> 00:06:26.986
THE OPPOSITION ORGANIZATION THAT

00:06:27.053 --> 00:06:27.987
REPRESENTS, A COHORT OF

00:06:28.054 --> 00:06:28.988
PSYCHIATRISTS TO TRY TO

00:06:29.055 --> 00:06:30.823
UNDERSTAND AND ADDRESS THEIR

00:06:30.890 --> 00:06:32.625
CONCERNS AS WE CAN. THANK YOU.

00:06:32.692 --> 00:06:34.994
THANK YOU, MA'AM. MR. CHAIRMAN

00:06:35.061 --> 00:06:35.995
RANDALL HAGER FOR THE

00:06:36.062 --> 00:06:37.430
PSYCHIATRIC PHYSICIANS ALLIANCE

